#Example2

Same as Example, but the import is moved into the body code block
instead of the post-text references section, as a workaround. Here the
author can control blank-line spacing directly, unlike in the
post-text references section.

    import math


    def double(n: int) -> int:
        return n * 2 + math.trunc(0.0)

~example
    double(21) == 42
